This corresponds to the first CRAN submission of the package.

All four checks included CRAN incoming remote checks, examples, unit tests,
vignette rebuilding, and the PDF and HTML reference manuals. Each environment
passed 1,365 test expectations, with no failures, warnings or skipped tests.

The first Linux R-devel attempt failed during R installation because Ubuntu
repository downloads failed. No package checks ran in that failed job.
Re-running only that job succeeded without changes to the source or workflow;
the successful re-run checked the original source archive.

